 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "현재진행형 (am / is / are + -ing)",
   "en": "Present continuous (am / is / are + -ing)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "지금 하고 있는 일은 am / is / are + 동사-ing로 말합니다: I am studying. 부정은 am / is / are 뒤에 not을 씁니다. 질문은 be동사를 앞으로 보냅니다: Are you studying? 철자: write → writing, run → running.",
   "en": "Say what is happening now with am / is / are + verb-ing: I am studying. For the negative put not after am / is / are. For a question put be first: Are you studying? Spelling: write → writing, run → running."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "긍정",
     "I am studying."
    ],
    [
     "부정",
     "He isn't reading."
    ],
    [
     "의문문",
     "Are you studying?"
    ],
    [
     "철자 변화",
     "write → writing, run → running"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "e로 끝나면 e를 빼고 -ing: write → writing.",
    "en": "If a verb ends in e, drop it and add -ing: write → writing."
   },
   {
    "ko": "하나의 모음 + 하나의 자음이면 자음을 겹쳐 씁니다: run → running.",
    "en": "One vowel + one consonant: double the consonant: run → running."
   },
   {
    "ko": "now, right now 같은 말과 자주 함께 써요.",
    "en": "It often goes with now and right now."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
